        <h2>Overview</h2>

        <p>
            The Bigfoot is a very tall, huge bear-like creature that live in Woodlands, it is said that it has a high-pitched scream
            that was recorded in 1972 in Sierra Nevada.
        </p>

        <h2>Appearance</h2>

        <p>
           The bigfoot is described as a bipedal primate standing 6 to 15 feet tall, and covered in dark brown or black fur.
        </p>

        <h2>Habitat</h2>

        <p>
            Large dense Woodlands.
        </p>

        <h2>Reported sightings</h2>

        <ul>
            <li>Sightings started around the mid-1900s following the discovery of large tracks by loggers in Northen
                California in 1958.
            </li>
        </ul>

        <h2>Theories</h2>

        <p>
            Some enthusiasts speculate Bigfoot could be a surviving descendent of Gigantopithecus, an extinct genus of massive, 
            ancient apes. While the mainstream scientific community does not recognize Bigfoot as a real animal.
            Most researchers believe sightings are misidentified black bears walking on their hind legs or elaborate hoaxes.
        </p>

